    "turn_idx": 6,
    "turn_text": "So, I see the legislature, your old stomping grounds. They went and went forward with the maps. Now, the congressional maps don't require governor approval. So, now it's just going to be up to the courts, which is one of your other stomping grounds as a lawyer. So, I'm kind of curious what your take is on where we stand now with the Supreme Court of the state of North Carolina. They get to pick some special masters. Or I'm sorry the lower court the trial court pick some special masters that they're going to do some apps you got plaintiffs they're drawn some maps in secret and you got these legislative maps have you I mean I know I'm sure you probably have looked at your district right to see where it where it's been drawn how it's been drawn so how do you fare in this and what do you think is going to happen now as you as it works its way through the next step of this process.",
